# Styling Conventions

## TailwindCSS Setup

The project uses TailwindCSS v3 with a custom theme configuration.

## cn() Utility

Location: `client/src/lib/utils.ts`

Always use `cn()` for className merging:

```typescript
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

// Basic usage
<div className={cn("base-class", className)} />

// Conditional classes
<div className={cn(
  "flex items-center gap-2",
  isActive && "bg-primary text-primary-foreground",
  isDisabled && "opacity-50 pointer-events-none",
  className
)} />

// With error states
<input className={cn(
  "flex h-10 w-full rounded-md border px-3 py-2",
  error && "border-destructive focus-visible:ring-destructive",
  className
)} />
```

## Theme Colors

The project uses CSS variables for theming (light/dark mode support):

### Semantic Colors

```typescript
// Primary colors
"bg-primary"              // Primary background
"text-primary"            // Primary text
"text-primary-foreground" // Text on primary background
"border-primary"          // Primary border

// Secondary
"bg-secondary"
"text-secondary"
"text-secondary-foreground"

// Destructive (errors, delete actions)
"bg-destructive"
"text-destructive"
"text-destructive-foreground"
"border-destructive"

// Muted (subtle backgrounds, disabled states)
"bg-muted"
"text-muted-foreground"

// Accent
"bg-accent"
"text-accent-foreground"

// Card backgrounds
"bg-card"
"text-card-foreground"

// Background and foreground
"bg-background"
"text-foreground"

// Borders
"border-border"
"border-input"
```

### Usage Examples

```typescript
// Button variants
<button className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground">Primary</button>
<button className="bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground">Delete</button>
<button className="bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground">Secondary</button>

// Cards
<div className="bg-card text-card-foreground border border-border rounded-lg p-4">
  Card content
</div>

// Subtle backgrounds
<div className="bg-muted text-muted-foreground p-2 rounded">
  Muted section
</div>

// Error states
<p className="text-destructive text-sm">Error message</p>
<input className="border-destructive" />
```

